  <Docs>
    <summary>Represents a single event in a vibration composition with a start time relative to the start of the composition.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>Represents a single event in a vibration composition with a start time relative to the start of the composition.</para>
      <para>An event is a self-contained vibration component with a specific starting point. Common examples include: A single Preset with a specific start time; A single Envelope with a specific start time; A legacy effect created via static VibrationEffect methods like VibrationEffect.createOneShot(long, int), VibrationEffect.createWaveform(long[], int[], int), VibrationEffect.createPredefined(int), etc., with a specific start time.</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/VibrationEffect.Event" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.os.VibrationEffect.Event</code>.</a></format></para>
